# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# routing.env — switches for the Routing Optimiser, loaded by run.command at startup.
#
# One per line, NAME=value. `#` starts a comment. Delete a line (or comment it out) to go back
# to the default. run.command echoes what it loaded, so the terminal always says which
# configuration a run used.
#
# EVERY optimisation in the engine ships behind one of these, so anything can be reverted without
# a code change. Only ONE of them changes the answer, and it is the first entry below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── THE ONE THAT CHANGES THE ANSWER ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# float32 band projector. Measured 1.598x on the projector on 2026-08-24 (15 of 15 paired rounds,
# p=0.000, against a +-2.0% floor), and the projector is ~34% of a generation, so ~20% of the
# search. It is ON here because a ~2-transaction drift on `txn` was accepted on 2026-08-24.
#
# TWO THINGS TO EXPECT IN THE LOG, both normal under this setting:
#   1. a *** FLOAT32 PROJECTOR IS ON banner, with the drift MEASURED on that run's own scaffold;
#   2. RECONCILIATION ERROR will no longer read 0. It is  sum|delivered - GA-fitness|, and
#      GA-fitness now comes from a float32 kernel while delivery stays float64, so it reads about
#      the drift. That is the setting, not a regression — but that number also stops being able
#      to detect a REAL reconciliation bug at that size. Set this to 0 to get the detector back.
# The search is chaotic, so a float32 run's trajectory differs from a float64 run's; compare end
# results, not candidate for candidate.
#
# HOW TO CONFIRM IT ACTUALLY ENGAGED (learned the expensive way on 2026-08-24). Setting the switch
# is not the same as the setting taking effect. On that run it WAS set, and a bug in the self-check
# above the banner raised, which disabled the whole cell-blocked path and took float32 down with it
# — silently, because the banner is printed after the line that raised. 5 h 22 m at the flat
# kernel's speed. Fixed in 19cd, and the failure line now says outright what it costs. So:
#   * search the log for FLOAT32 PROJECTOR IS ON. Present = it engaged. ABSENT = it did NOT,
#     whatever this file says.
#   * search for "could not run" and "FAILED to run". Either means the projector fell back to the
#     flat kernel and every timing below it is roughly half the engine's real speed.
ROUTING_PROJ_FLOAT32=1

# ── MEASUREMENT (read-only blocks; none of these touch the split) ─────────────────────────────
# Paired rounds for [stage-ab]. 11 by default since 19cc: at 7 the only sign-test scores that
# clear p<=0.10 are 7/7 and 0/7, so one unlucky round buries a real effect — which is what
# happened to the lanes row at +5.0%, 6/7. Raise further if a row still reads NOT MEASURABLE.
# ROUTING_STAGE_AB_REPS=11

# [kernel-ab] costs ~95 s and every one of its variants now has a standing verdict (C, D, E dead;
# F real but answer-moving; G and chunking adopted). Set to 0 to skip it and get that time back;
# set it back to 1 when a NEW kernel idea needs deciding.
# ROUTING_KERNEL_AB=0

# ── REVERTS (each turns off one shipped optimisation; all are bit-identical either way) ───────
# ROUTING_SOFTMAX_FUSE=0     # 19bx fused softmax        -> the untouched numpy reference
# ROUTING_CHILD_FUSE=0       # 19bx fused child          -> crossover + _mutate_fast, separately
# ROUTING_DELIV_FUSE=0       # 19ca scatter-into-cap     -> scatter, copy, cap
# ROUTING_ELIG_FUSE=0        # 19bs fused eligibility    -> the 19bm numpy chain
# ROUTING_PROJ_CELLBLOCK=0   # 19bt cell-blocked kernel  -> the flat kernel
# ROUTING_PROJ_LANES=8       # 19by lane cap             -> 8 (16 is the shipped default)
# ROUTING_ROW_PARALLEL=0     # 19bn threading of deliver + softmax
# ROUTING_MUT_FAST=0         # 19bp sparse mutation draws — NOTE this one CHANGES THE SEARCH back
#                            # to the pre-19bp random sample, and forces the child fusion off too.
